<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n51254" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vŏcātor</span></b> ,
		ōris, m.
		id. (post-Aug.), <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>a caller.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b> In gen.: Paulus vocator
			gentium, Prud. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στεφ</span>. 2, 461;
					<i><span class="en">Ambros. in Luc. 3, §
			33</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			In partic., <i>a bidder</i>, <i>inviter</i> to dinner, etc., <i><span class="en">Sen.
				Ira, 3, 37, 3</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 35, 10, 36, § 89</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">Suet. Calig. 39</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Mart. 7,
				85, 11</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
